# Example override file: it replaces package versions of the image, for example
# for a GPU that the CUDA build of the image does not support.
#
# How it works: the container passes this file to uv as an override file.
# Each version here replaces the version of the image. The container installs
# all packages into /data/venv once. Later starts install nothing.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file into your data folder:
#        cp user_requirements.txt.example ./data/user_requirements.txt
#   2. Set the environment variables (the path is INSIDE the container):
#        UV_OVERRIDE=/data/user_requirements.txt
#        UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL=<the index of the section, if it names one>
#   3. Uncomment ONE of the sections below and restart the container.
#
# To remove a package of the image, give it a marker that is never true:
#   some-package ; sys_platform == "never"
#
# The CUDA image has these GPU packages:
#   onnxruntime-gpu 1.30.0: speech model, CUDA 13 and cuDNN 9 (nvidia-* packages
#     without the -cu12 suffix, and nvidia-cudnn-cu13).
#   ctranslate2 4.8.2: verbalizer, built with CUDA 12.8. It needs the CUDA 12
#     cuBLAS: nvidia-cublas-cu12 12.9.2.10 and nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12 12.9.79.
#     The image points LD_LIBRARY_PATH at them.
#
# For GTX 10xx (Pascal, sm_61). Not tested on a Pascal GPU.
# CUDA 13 does not support GPUs older than Turing, so the speech model needs the
# CUDA 12 build of onnxruntime-gpu. It has the same name and version as the
# CUDA 13 build on PyPI, but it comes from the CUDA 12 index of ONNX Runtime:
#   UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL=https://aiinfra.pkgs.visualstudio.com/PublicPackages/_packaging/onnxruntime-cuda-12/pypi/simple/
# cuDNN 9.11 and later do not support GPUs older than Turing.
# nvidia-cudnn-cu12 and nvidia-cudnn-cu13 write the same files, so remove the cu13 one.
# The verbalizer uses int8_float16 on the GPU, and Pascal cannot run it. Also set:
#   VERBALIZER_DEVICE=cpu
# onnxruntime-gpu[cuda,cudnn]==1.29.0
# nvidia-cudnn-cu12==9.10.2.21
# nvidia-cudnn-cu13 ; sys_platform == "never"
# nvidia-cublas ; sys_platform == "never"
# nvidia-cuda-runtime ; sys_platform == "never"
# nvidia-cuda-nvrtc ; sys_platform == "never"
# nvidia-cufft ; sys_platform == "never"
# nvidia-curand ; sys_platform == "never"
# nvidia-nvjitlink ; sys_platform == "never"
#
# For RTX 50xx (Blackwell, sm_120): the versions of the image support it, so no
# override is necessary. Not tested on a Blackwell GPU. If you pin older
# versions, keep at least these:
# onnxruntime-gpu>=1.28.0
# ctranslate2>=4.7.0
# nvidia-cublas-cu12>=12.8.3.14
#
# Another version of the same CUDA 13 build, for example to go back after a
# problem with a new release (tested on an RTX 4090):
# onnxruntime-gpu==1.29.0
